    },
    {
      "text": "The model explicitly represents oxygen doping and defect scattering.",
      "field": "hypothesis",
      "needs_support": true,
      "support": "unsupported",
      "supporting_ids": [],
      "same_system": "na"
    },
    {
      "text": "The model separately predicts lattice and electronic thermal-conductivity contributions in HfNbTaTiZr.",
      "field": "hypothesis",
      "needs_support": true,
      "support": "partial",
      "supporting_ids": [
        "PMC4735586::web::005::body",
        "PMC9822225::web::003::1_introduction"
      ],
      "same_system": "unclear"
    },
    {
      "text": "The model will predict measurements over 100–1200 K for HfNbTaTiZr containing up to about 1 wt.% oxygen.",
      "field": "hypothesis",
      "needs_support": true,
      "support": "unsupported",
      "supporting_ids": [],
      "same_system": "na"
    },
    {
      "text": "The model will reduce prediction error by approximately 20–30% relative to Debye-based or perfect-crystal approaches.",
      "field": "hypothesis",
      "needs_support": true,
      "support": "unsupported",
      "supporting_ids": [],
      "same_system": "na"
    },
    {
      "text": "The relevant initial material is near-equiatomic HfNbTaTiZr with up to about 1 wt.% oxygen.",
      "field": "material_initial_state",
      "needs_support": true,
      "support": "unsupported",
      "supporting_ids": [],
      "same_system": "na"
    },
    {
      "text": "Such samples contain typical point defects and slight compositional inhomogeneities.",
      "field": "material_initial_state",
      "needs_support": true,
      "support": "unsupported",
      "supporting_ids": [],
      "same_system": "na"
    },
    {
      "text": "The proposed approach integrates ab initio data, experimental references, and explicit electron–phonon scattering terms.",
      "field": "intervention",
      "needs_support": false,
      "support": "partial",
      "supporting_ids": [
        "PMC9822225::web::003::1_introduction",
        "PMC9323025::web::022::4_conclusions"
      ],
      "same_system": "no"
    },
    {
      "text": "The ML surrogates incorporate local lattice distortions, defect scattering, and partial phase or compositional inhomogeneity.",
