      "needs_support": false,
      "support": "partial",
      "supporting_ids": [
        "PMC11136967::web::000::abstract",
        "PMC9822225::web::003::1_introduction"
      ],
      "same_system": "no"
    },
    {
      "text": "Chemical complexity, point defects, and oxidation produce scattering contributions relevant to heat transport.",
      "field": "mechanism",
      "needs_support": true,
      "support": "partial",
      "supporting_ids": [
        "PMC11136967::web::000::abstract",
        "PMC9822225::web::003::1_introduction"
      ],
      "same_system": "no"
    },
    {
      "text": "Representing those scattering contributions enables accurate separation of lattice and electronic conduction paths.",
      "field": "mechanism",
      "needs_support": true,
      "support": "unsupported",
      "supporting_ids": [],
      "same_system": "na"
    },
    {
      "text": "Previous approaches conflated phonon and electronic thermal-transport contributions.",
      "field": "baseline",
      "needs_support": true,
      "support": "unsupported",
      "supporting_ids": [],
      "same_system": "na"
    },
    {
      "text": "Previous approaches treated only idealized crystal structures.",
      "field": "baseline",
      "needs_support": true,
      "support": "unsupported",
      "supporting_ids": [],
      "same_system": "na"
    },
    {
      "text": "Previous approaches relied on simplified Debye-temperature approximations.",
      "field": "baseline",
      "needs_support": true,
      "support": "unsupported",
      "supporting_ids": [],
      "same_system": "na"
    },
    {
      "text": "Previous approaches had discrepancies exceeding 25–30% relative to measured thermal conductivity.",
      "field": "baseline",
      "needs_support": true,
      "support": "unsupported",
      "supporting_ids": [],
      "same_system": "na"
    },
    {
      "text": "The proposed model is expected to be reliable only for near-equiatomic HfNbTaTiZr with oxygen additions up to about 1 wt.%.",
